# Context

## Background
T090 restores the CI and Build artifacts gates that failed at 2945a4a.
Both workflows had never passed on the current workflow files: CI failed
on Node 20 and on Windows, and Build artifacts failed in the zig setup of
both cross builds, so the packages and install jobs never ran.

## Why This Way
- Node 20 V8 states only "at position N" in a JSON parse failure; the
  line and column suffix starts with Node 22. The product now derives
  "line L column C" from the stated position, so the invalid_json
  contract holds on every declared Node version and the test assertion
  stays unchanged. The derivation counts newlines before the position,
  which matches the V8 convention on every probed input.
- Windows reports backslashes from the fixture walk while manifest paths
  state forward slashes; one normalization in fixtureJsonFiles fixes all
  five failing fixture tests without touching their assertions.
- Windows checkouts converted text files to CRLF, which broke the
  byte-exact export comparisons and the per-line heading regex of the
  documentation link check. .gitattributes enforces LF, because the
  exports and hashing fixtures are byte-exact contracts.
- The zig failure had two layers: mlugg/setup-zig@v1 requests the
  pre-0.14 archive names, so every download 404s; after the v2 upgrade,
  zig 0.16.0 mishandles the separate "-Wl,-exported_symbols_list"
  arguments of cargo-zigbuild 0.23.4 on the darwin link. 1fd836a pins
  zig 0.15.2, which links both cross targets with 0.23.4.

